# Engineering Tools reads no environment file at the moment.
#
# Every variable that used to be here — DATABASE_URL, SESSION_SECRET,
# BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_*, SEED_TEST_USER_* — belonged to the identity stack, which
# is MAEC One Core's now and has its own .env.example. Nothing in this
# service replaced them: the only environment it reads is RENDER and
# MAEC_DEV, and both are set by the platform or the shell, never by a file.
# python-dotenv went with the identity package for the same reason.
#
# The file is kept, empty, because it is about to be needed again. The OIDC
# client will want roughly:
#
#   MAEC_CORE_ISSUER=https://auth.mirageaec.com
#   MAEC_CLIENT_ID=engineering-tools
#   MAEC_CLIENT_SECRET=            # server-to-server code exchange only
#
# Those are sketched, not settled — see OPEN-DECISIONS #11, which has to be
# decided before any of them means anything.
